            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DWILSON0116"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been making this dip for a couple of years with the following adjustments: Use light Strawberry Cream Cheese. I add 2 TBS of orange juice when mixing with the marshmallow ceam. Finally, I fold in 1 cup of Cool Whip. I never have any left overs with this dip!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CAPEMOM77"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think this stuff is AWESOME!!! You couldn't have a simpler recipe. Two ingredients, people!!! It tastes too good. I make this for just about any gathering at my house, because it always gets eaten. Just remember to let your cream cheese soften before you mix. It is a lot easier this way. Also I stick my rubber scraper in very hot water to help to get the sticky marshmallow cream out of the jar. Enjoy!",
            "datePublished": "2006-12-30T21:42:01.377Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MICKE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used strawberry cream cheese, added 1 cup of cool whip and 2 tbsp orange juice. Had people at the party eating dip without the fruit it was so good. Thanks for the great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2002-10-06T09:32:05.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is basically the same fruit dip my family has made for years, except we add 1/4 t sugar and 1/2 vanilla extract. We also add a few drops of red food coloring to give it a pink hue. This makes it so pretty next to strawberries, watermelon, cantaloupe and fresh pineapple chunks",
            "datePublished": "2002-02-19T11:34:45.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CHRISTINE B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good. If you add cool whip make sure the cream cheese and marshmallow creme are mixed well first. Serve with a fruit and bite size cubes of pound cake! Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2002-10-22T15:24:00.467Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this recipe all of the time, but I add a few drops of marachino (sp)cherry juice to make it have a pink tint. Its great with strawberries",
            "datePublished": "2002-10-10T14:43:06.653Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shannon D"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe. I usually add about 1-2T lemon juice. It makes it smoother, and it gives it just a little bit of a kick. Either way, this is a great dip for any kind of fruit...melons, berries, grapes, bananas, you name it!",
            "datePublished": "2002-08-01T10:09:49.873Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MICHELE B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Every since I made this receipe for the first time a couple of months ago I get requests for it all the time! My son loves it and I have served it at several get-togethers. Sometimes I add a bit of orange juice and I always use light strawberry cream cheese.",
            "datePublished": "2003-03-25T16:56:12.047Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Beth Dziagwa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have used this recipe for a few years now but I have varied it several times. You can use any kind of the sweet flavored cream cheeses or make it with the marshmallow cream and 8 oz cream cheese and add 3 tablespoons of cocoa powder to it to make the best chocolate fruit dip ever!!! P.S. You can also use this as an icing on cake!",
            "datePublished": "2008-05-15T12:18:36.893Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sarahiswright"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect with any fruit, and I love the consistency! I agree with other reviewers who doubled the recipe - it's a must. I also added a few tablespoons of powdered sugar, a splash of vanilla, and food coloring. If you're out of marshmallow creme, you can melt 16 oz. marshmallows with 3 1/2 Tbsp. corn syrup and use that instead. You can't tell the difference!",
            "datePublished": "2005-08-11T14:22:10.983Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "aolink"
            },
            "reviewBody": "4 stars as written. but 5 stars after following other reviewers suggestions. i used strawberry cream cheese, cool whip, and orange juice. awesome! strawberries and bananas are amazing with this dip!",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-23T15:53:08.753Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rhondarr"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Have made this for years. Recently wanted something different than caramel for fruit. Grandkids disagreed as their friends “ won’t eat it”. I made it just as some of the teenagers arrived. They were interested at how fast I made it without a mixer. After the party there was nothing left of it and they ate only a small amount of caramel dip from the market. Two even asked for the recipe before leaving. Even old standbys can be enjoyed by the new generation",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-15T10:51:02.602Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dash"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added blueberry jam to give it added flavor! It was delicious! I'll make it again using another flavor of jam or jelly! Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2026-06-24T10:45:26.867Z"
          },
          {
